<title>NETHERLANDS: Hankyu to move to Schiphol Southeast.</title>
<headline>Hankyu to move to Schiphol Southeast.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Work has started on on new facilities for Japanese forwarder, Hankyu International Transport at Amsterdam Schiphol, an airport statement said.</p>
<p>Based at Cargo World Schiphol Southeast, the site includes a 2000 sq m warehouse and 730 sq m of office space and is due to on December 9 this year.</p>
<p>At present, Hankyu is based at the Freightway building at Schiphol South and it will become the third company to move to the new Schiphol Southeast building.</p>
<p>This is reserved for forwarders and companies specialising in logistic services and is being developed by Schiphol Real Estate at a cost of four million guilders. -Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542-7706 Fax+5017</p>
